      "name": null,
      "problem": "Express $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta +{31}^{∘})$ as a cofunction of a complementary angle.",
      "worked_solution": "We know that the cofunction of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ is $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ and the angle complementary to $\\theta +{31}^{∘}$ is \n\n$$\n{90}^{∘}-(\\theta +{31}^{∘})={90}^{∘}-\\theta -{31}^{∘}={59}^{∘}-\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta +{31}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({90}^{∘}-(\\theta +{31}^{∘}))=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({59}^{∘}-\\theta ).\n$$",
